15461718"],"issn_org":["10614036"],"issue":"5","journal":"Nature Genetics","pages":"560-572","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Genetics","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130637871"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c311f054-cd8c-47bd-a7ee-60cf4940ce8d","au-04d034b2-c833-41e4-8665-f9fb146b8f52","ku-0f852390-b1f2-4e06-8025-9442c43a33a0","sdu-912310f1-1215-4cf9-b624-a07928417dff"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Multi-ancestry genetic study of type 2 diabetes highlights the power of diverse populations for discovery and translation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-088.44-009381","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We present an overview of results from a series of L-H transition experiments undertaken at JET since the installation of the ITER-like-wall (JET-ILW), with beryllium wall tiles and a tungsten divertor. Tritium, helium and deuterium plasmas have been investigated. Initial results in tritium show ohmic L-H transitions at low density and the power threshold for the L-H transition (PLH) is lower in tritium plasmas than in deuterium ones at low densities, while we still lack contrasted data to provide a scaling at high densities. In helium plasmas there is a notable shift of the density at which the power threshold is minimum ( ¯ne,min ) to higher values relative to deuterium and hydrogen references. Above ¯ne,min (He) the L-H power threshold at high densities is similar for D and He plasmas. Transport modelling in slab geometry shows that in helium neoclassical transport competes with interchange-driven transport, unlike in hydrogen isotopes. Measurements of the radial electric field in deuterium plasmas show that Er shear is not a good indicator of proximity to the L-H transition. Transport analysis of ion heat flux in deuterium plasmas show a non-linearity as density is decreased below ¯ne,min. Lastly, a regression of the JET-ILW deuterium data is compared to the 2008 ITPA scaling law.","author_count":77,"contributors":["Solano, E. R.","Delabie, E.","Birkenmeier, G.","Silva, C.","Hillesheim, J. C.","Vincenzi, P.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Baciero, A.","Aleiferis, S.","Balboa, I.","Boboc, A.","Bourdelle, C.","Carvalho, I. S.","Carvalho, P.","Chernyshova, M.","Coelho, R.","Craciunescu, T.","Dumont, R.","Dumortier, P.","Luna, E. De La","Flanagan, J.","Fontana, M.","Fontdecaba, J. M.","Frassinetti, L.","Gallart, D.","Garcia, J.","Giovannozzi, E.","Giroud, C.","Gromelski, W.","Henriques, R.","Horvath, L.","Jacquet, P.","Jepu, I.","Kappatou, A.","Keeling, D. L.","King, D.","Kowalska-Strzȩciwilk, E.","Lennholm, M.","Lerche, E.","Litherland